{title: Let Us with a Gladsome Mind}
{artist: John Milton / John Antes}
{genre: Hymn, Psalm}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 113}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns Ancient and Modern, standard edition (Norfolk, England: Canterbury Press, 1994),# 381)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Let [Am]us, [G]with [C]a [F]glad[Dm]some [C]mind,
[C]Praise the [G]Lord, for He is kind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]For His mercies [C]aye en[G]dure,
[C]Ever [G7]faithful, ever [C]sure.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Let [Am]us [G]blaze [C]His [F]name [Dm]ab[C]road,
[C]For of [G]gods He is the God.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]He [Am]with [G]all [C]com[F]mand[Dm]ing [C]might
[C]Filled the [G]new made world with light.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]He [Am]the [G]gold[C]en [F]tress[Dm]èd [C]sun
[C]Caused all [G]day his course to run.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[C]Th’hor[Am]nèd [G]moon [C]to [F]shine [Dm]by [C]night;
[C]’Mid her [G]spangled sisters bright.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[C]All [Am]things [G]liv[C]ing [F]He [Dm]doth [C]feed,
[C]His full [G]hand supplies their need.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[C]Let [Am]us, [G]with [C]a [F]glad[Dm]some [C]mind,
[C]Praise the [G]Lord, for He is kind.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
